Trans:
The Ukrainian Ministry of Health publishes guidelines on how to use generators to avoid life-threatening dangers:

- Generators and fuel should be used **only outdoors, at least 6 meters away from windows, doors, and garages;**
- Keep the generator **dry and protected from rain and flooding.** Contact with a wet generator or devices connected to it can result in electric shock;
- Allow the generator to cool down before refueling. Fuel spilled on hot engine parts can ignite;
- Install **carbon monoxide detectors** in the room;
- Always **purchase a fire extinguisher and keep it in a visible and easily accessible location.**

