Trans:
The unemployed will be required to perform public works. They will be paid the minimum wage — [Ministry of Economy](https://www.me.gov.ua/News/Detail?lang=uk-UA&id=1455dd6f-3083-4891-af96-00ed9c7c497a&title=Bezrobitni)

Due to the war, it is expected that the unemployment rate will be high by year-end — around 30% — so the government proposes a mechanism where the unemployed can be engaged in:
- setting up roadblocks, cutting trees for trench digging;
- gathering firewood for military and civilian use;
- clearing debris and repairing homes damaged as a result of combat operations;
- reinforcing dikes;
- clearing roads from debris;
- unloading humanitarian aid;
- preparing shelters;
- repairs and restoration of facilities in the social sphere;
- assisting vulnerable persons, people with disabilities, and the elderly.

Such work is already being performed by the unemployed in Sumy and Chernihiv regions.

